# Release signing template for DroidCar
#
# Usage:
#   1) Copy this file to keystore.properties in the repository root (that file is excluded in .gitignore).
#   2) Create a key with keytool (or use your existing one):
#        keytool -genkeypair -v -keystore droidcar-release.jks \
#          -alias droidcar -keyalg RSA -keysize 4096 -validity 10000
#   3) Fill in the four values below and put the keystore in the repository root (or use an absolute path).
#   4) ./gradlew :app:assembleStandardRelease -Pdroidcar.buildNumber=$(git rev-list --count HEAD)
#        -> app/build/outputs/apk/standard/release/app-standard-release.apk
#   5) Check with apksigner that the certificate CN is NOT "Android Debug":
#        $ANDROID_HOME/build-tools/<ver>/apksigner verify --print-certs <apk>
#
# A leaked private key lets anyone ship updates that install over yours: never commit or share the keystore or its
# passwords. A lost key means no more updates for existing users (everyone has to uninstall and reinstall), and a
# published certificate cannot be changed for the same reason. Store the passwords in a password manager right away.

storeFile=droidcar-release.jks
storePassword=CHANGE_ME
keyAlias=droidcar
keyPassword=CHANGE_ME
